# ESP-Hosted NG NuttX staging

This directory stages the ESP-Hosted NG source import used by the
FeatherCore_ESP STM32H7S78-DK + ESP32-C5 Wi-Fi bring-up.

- `upstream/` is copied from `third/esp-hosted/esp_hosted_ng`.
- The ESP32-C5 firmware is built from `upstream/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter`.
- The original host driver under `upstream/host` is a Linux kernel module.
- NuttX host-side glue is tracked under
  `nuttx/drivers/wireless/esp_hosted_ng`.

The SPI firmware flashed to ESP32-C5 must be configured with:

```text
CONFIG_ESP_SPI_HOST_INTERFACE=y
# CONFIG_ESP_SDIO_HOST_INTERFACE is not set
```

## Current NuttX host-side status

The STM32H7S78-DK `nsh-esp_hosted_ng` build now includes:

- `nuttx/drivers/wireless/esp_hosted_ng/esp_hosted_ng_netdev.c`
  registers `CONFIG_WL_ESP_HOSTED_NG_IFNAME`, normally `wlan0`, as a
  NuttX wireless netdev lower-half.
- `nuttx/drivers/wireless/esp_hosted_ng/esp_hosted_ng_transport.c`
  provides the ESP-Hosted NG SPI frame boundary: 1600-byte full-duplex
  transfers, ESP payload header creation, STA data frame wrapping, and a
  weak board hook named `esp_hosted_ng_spibus_initialize()`.
- `apps/examples/esp32_wifi_demo` is available from NSH and drives the
  interface through WEXT-style ioctls:

```text
nsh> esp32_wifi_demo status
nsh> esp32_wifi_demo up
nsh> esp32_wifi_demo connect <ssid>
nsh> esp32_wifi_demo ip
nsh> esp32_wifi_demo all <ssid>
```

At this point the image is intentionally honest about the remaining hardware
gap.  The current STM32H7RS NuttX tree contains XSPI support for external
memory, but does not yet provide a regular STM32H7RS SPI master lower-half.
Until that exists and the board overrides `esp_hosted_ng_spibus_initialize()`,
`esp32_wifi_demo connect` will fail with `-ENODEV` after `wlan0` is registered.

The next board bring-up step is therefore:

1. Add or enable a normal STM32H7RS SPI master driver.
2. Bind the ESP32-C5 chip-select, handshake, data-ready, and optional reset
   GPIOs in `stm32h7s78-dk`.
3. Implement the board hook:

```c
FAR struct spi_dev_s *esp_hosted_ng_spibus_initialize(int bus)
{
  return stm32h7rs_spibus_initialize(bus);
}
```

4. Replace the polling-only transport skeleton with handshake/data-ready IRQ
   scheduling and command response handling equivalent to ESP-Hosted NG
   `upstream/host/spi/esp_spi.c`.
